Suggests: linuxcnc-doc-en
Description: touch-first HMI for LinuxCNC
 LiNC is a Rust/egui control-panel HMI for LinuxCNC. It reads machine state and
 issues only explicit, validated commands (MDI, probe, tool change, program and
 offset writes); the physical CNC panel remains authoritative for mode, cycle,
 jog, spindle and coolant.
 .
 The package ships four programs:
 .
  * linc        - the display/HMI window
  * linc-panel  - the panel service (RS-485 or simulator), run separately so a
                  UI crash cannot remove panel control
  * linc-mcp    - a read-only diagnostic server for agents, over a same-user
                  Unix socket
  * linc-plc    - a userspace ladder PLC service with its own linc_plc.* HAL
                  component, started by the machine HAL rather than the HMI
 .
 Example profiles are installed under /usr/share/linc; a machine profile is
 supplied by the machine vendor and selected with --config or LINC_CONFIG.
